<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_SekkulaathTank.xml                            FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_PRISON_1

  "A prison tank, not a pen: it teaches, it produces, and it can get out"
  (design sheet §6j/§6m, owner rulings 2026-09-23). 🔴 It is a CELL, not a
  pen — the occupant is a prisoner, not livestock ("Do not write, name or
  art this as animal husbandry"). Everything below is written to that: no
  "feed your animal" language, no husbandry flavour.

  RM_LivingCapturePodBase is the GENERIC abstraction the item's own `open`
  list asked this build to decide ("what the generic abstraction actually
  is... it is the first real decision of the build"): one abstract Building
  ThingDef + one parameterised comp (RM_CompProperties_CapturedSpecimen),
  never a bespoke class per captive species. 4a's own named candidates
  (venom creature, egg-layer, blood donor, nectar-drinker) are meant to
  ParentName off THIS base with a different occupant/product set, not a new
  ThingDef hierarchy.

  Feeding rides vanilla CompRefuelable (fuelFilter: any MeatRaw item) rather
  than new hauling/UI code — WorkGiver_Refuel already delivers meat to any
  refuelable building with no bespoke job. "Fed corpses or meat" (§6j):
  corpses are deliberately NOT wired as fuel here (CompRefuelable's fuel
  value model does not fit a Corpse Thing cleanly) — a documented scope cut,
  not an open design question; meat alone already satisfies "fed... it
  yields the product line."

  Escape triggers (RM_CompCapturedSpecimen): sustained neglect (empty fuel
  past a threshold, then an MTB roll) OR damage past a threshold fraction
  (a flat per-hit chance) — "a neglected OR damaged tank releases it" (§6j).
  Tank materials, feed rate, and the damage threshold are INVENTED
  placeholders (flagged per-field on the comp) — FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_TANK_TUNING_1
  owes the real numbers, same posture as the tentacle bestiary's own
  FEVERWOOD_TENTACLE_SETPIECE_TUNING_1.

  No researchPrerequisites: the design doc names none for the tank, and
  none was invented.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: one flat-color 128x128 PNG. Searched artpipe done/
  registry.jsonl for "tank"/"prison"/"sekkulaath"/"dianoga" first (standing
  rule) — nothing for a containment vessel exists; canon_dianoga_v1_* is the
  Star Wars-tier creature art, a different asset for a different tier.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef Name="RM_LivingCapturePodBase" ParentName="BuildingBase" Abstract="true">
    <size>(2,2)</size>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>1.0</fillPercent>
    <coversFloor>false</coversFloor>
    <useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <designationCategory>Production</designationCategory>
    <constructEffect>ConstructMetal</constructEffect>
    <statBases>
      <!-- INVENTED tank-materials placeholders — see file header. -->
      <WorkToBuild>2200</WorkToBuild>
      <MaxHitPoints>260</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.2</Flammability>
      <Beauty>-6</Beauty>
      <Cleanliness>-2</Cleanliness>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <Steel>90</Steel>
      <WoodLog>40</WoodLog>
      <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <building>
      <claimable>true</claimable>
      <deconstructible>true</deconstructible>
    </building>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_LivingCapturePodBase">
    <defName>RM_SekkulaathTank</defName>
    <label>sekkulaath prison tank</label>
    <description>A sealed, waterlogged cell, not a pen. Whatever is inside it did not agree to be there and is strong enough that it never has to — the tank holds because it is built to, not because the occupant tolerates it. Fed, it will produce; neglected or breached, it will not stay.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/RM_SekkulaathTank/RM_SekkulaathTank</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,2)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Refuelable">
        <!-- INVENTED feed-rate placeholders — see file header. -->
        <fuelConsumptionRate>3</fuelConsumptionRate>
        <fuelCapacity>15</fuelCapacity>
        <initialFuelPercent>0.5</initialFuelPercent>
        <fuelFilter>
          <categories>
            <li>MeatRaw</li>
          </categories>
        </fuelFilter>
        <destroyOnNoFuel>false</destroyOnNoFuel>
        <showAllowAutoRefuelToggle>true</showAllowAutoRefuelToggle>
        <fuelGizmoLabel>Occupant fed</fuelGizmoLabel>
        <fuelLabel>meat stock</fuelLabel>
        <targetFuelLevelConfigurable>false</targetFuelLevelConfigurable>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.FeverWood.RM_CompProperties_CapturedSpecimen">
        <occupantKindDefName>RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile</occupantKindDefName>
        <neglectDaysBeforeEscapeRisk>3</neglectDaysBeforeEscapeRisk>
        <neglectEscapeMtbDays>4</neglectEscapeMtbDays>
        <damageEscapeThresholdFraction>0.5</damageEscapeThresholdFraction>
        <damageEscapeChancePerHit>0.35</damageEscapeChancePerHit>
        <teachesColonyWarning>true</teachesColonyWarning>
        <products>
          <li>
            <thing>RM_SeveredTentacleFlesh</thing>
            <mtbDays>3</mtbDays>
            <countRange>1~2</countRange>
          </li>
          <li>
            <thing>RM_SekkulaathSpleenChemicals</thing>
            <mtbDays>5</mtbDays>
            <countRange>1~2</countRange>
          </li>
          <li>
            <thing>RM_SekkulaathCream</thing>
            <mtbDays>4</mtbDays>
            <countRange>1~3</countRange>
          </li>
        </products>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
